                <pb facs="0308" n="218" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg218"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.05/162: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-11T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 11, 1920—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>638. Your 887, June 3, 5 p.m., regarding judicial reforms in Egypt.</p>
                <p>Department sees no objection at present to suggestion that negotiations be
                    conducted in London.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
